     boot-mount gate is triggered, because no tool schema changed.
  3. That the pass never misfires on real-world prose. The bound is STATED, not measured: it separates a
     wrapped line from a deliberate column-0 continuation by delimiter evidence plus the uniqueness gate,
     so prose carrying a genuinely unmatched bracket followed by an unindented line can read as a
     candidate. It never deletes, never reorders, and never fires on a block it cannot decide. A
     corpus-scale false-positive sweep over real repositories was NOT run.
  4. Any behavioural equivalence with the replaced core. That is not a goal: contract §0 constraint 1
     declares such a criterion invalid, and the SUL-1.0-derived bytes were never opened.
